# Feature Request: Enterprise File Management System for Smart UI Analysis

## Objective

Redesign the file upload and storage system of the Smart UI Analysis application to support **multiple file uploads**, **all common file formats**, and **permanent backend storage**.

The system must ensure that **uploaded files are never permanently deleted from the backend**, even if the user deletes them from the frontend.

---

# 1. Multiple File Upload

Allow users to upload:

* Single file
* Multiple files
* Drag & Drop multiple files
* Folder upload (optional)

Supported formats:

### Images

* PNG
* JPG
* JPEG
* GIF
* BMP
* TIFF
* WEBP
* SVG

### Documents

* PDF
* DOC
* DOCX
* XLS
* XLSX
* PPT
* PPTX
* TXT
* CSV
* XML
* JSON
* RTF
* ODT

### Archives (Optional)

* ZIP
* RAR
* 7Z

The application must automatically detect the file type and validate supported formats.

---

# 2. Project-Based Backend Storage

Every uploaded project must automatically create a dedicated folder on the backend.

Example:

```text
/uploads/

    Banking_Project/

        Dashboard.png

        Login_Page.png

        Employee.pdf

        Invoice.pdf

        Requirements.docx

        Report.xlsx

        metadata.json

    HRMS_Project/

        Login.png

        EmployeeList.pdf

        Attendance.xlsx

        OCR_Report.pdf
```

Folder name should be:

```
<Project_Name>
```

If the project name already exists:

```
<Project_Name>_1

<Project_Name>_2

<Project_Name>_3
```

or use

```
<ProjectID>_<ProjectName>
```

to avoid conflicts.

---

# 3. Backend File Storage

Every uploaded file must be permanently stored on the backend.

Never overwrite existing files.

Store:

* Original File Name
* Stored File Name
* Project Name
* Upload Date
* File Size
* File Type
* Uploaded By
* File Path
* File ID

Example:

```text
Project Name:
HRMS

Original File:
Dashboard.png

Stored File:
20260705153020_Dashboard.png

Path:
/uploads/HRMS/

File Type:
PNG
```

---

# 4. Frontend Delete Behavior

When the user clicks Delete in the UI:

❌ Do NOT physically delete the file from the backend.

Instead:

* Remove it only from the project view.
* Mark it as deleted in the database.

Example:

```text
status = DELETED
```

or

```text
isDeleted = true
```

The actual file must remain inside the backend storage folder.

This ensures data recovery and audit history.

---

# 5. Restore Deleted Files

Provide an option:

```
Restore Deleted Files
```

The application should restore the file from backend storage without requiring another upload.

---

# 6. Permanent Backend Archive

Even if:

* User deletes the file
* User deletes the project
* User logs out

The backend folder and original uploaded files must remain unchanged.

Only database status should change.

Example:

```text
Project Deleted

↓

Database

status = ARCHIVED

↓

Files

Remain inside

/uploads/ProjectName/
```

---

# 7. Download Storage

Whenever any file is uploaded:

Automatically save an exact copy inside the project folder.

Example:

```text
/uploads/

HRMS/

    Login.png

    Dashboard.png

    Employee.pdf

    Requirement.docx
```

These files become the permanent master copies.

---

# 8. Project Metadata

Create a metadata file inside every project folder.

Example:

```text
/uploads/

HRMS/

    metadata.json
```

Contents:

```json
{
  "projectId": "PRJ-0001",
  "projectName": "HRMS",
  "manager": "manager@app.com",
  "createdDate": "2026-07-05",
  "totalFiles": 12,
  "deletedFiles": 2,
  "activeFiles": 10
}
```

---

# 9. OCR Storage

Whenever OCR is completed:

Save:

```
uploads/

HRMS/

OCR/

Login_Page.json

Dashboard.json

Employee_Page_1.json
```

Example:

```json
{
    "file":"Dashboard.png",
    "page":1,
    "ocrText":"Dashboard\nEmployee Details\nLogout",
    "confidence":98.7
}
```

---

# 10. Generated Reports

Every generated report should also be saved permanently.

Example:

```text
uploads/

HRMS/

Reports/

Analysis_Report.pdf

OCR_Report.pdf

Summary_Report.pdf
```

Even if the user downloads or deletes the report from the UI, the backend copy must remain.

---

# 11. Database Design

Create tables:

### Projects

* Project ID
* Project Name
* Manager
* Folder Path
* Created Date
* Status

### Files

* File ID
* Project ID
* Original File Name
* Stored File Name
* File Type
* File Size
* Upload Date
* File Path
* isDeleted
* OCR Status

### Reports

* Report ID
* Project ID
* Report Name
* Report Path
* Generated Date

---

# 12. Security

Only authenticated managers can:

* Upload files
* Download files
* Generate reports
* View project files

Backend storage must not be publicly accessible.

All file access should go through secured REST APIs.

---

# 13. Performance

* Upload multiple files simultaneously.
* Store files asynchronously.
* Prevent duplicate uploads using checksum/hash validation.
* Support files up to **100 MB** each.
* Support **1,000+ files** per project.
* Generate thumbnails for images.
* Render PDFs using **PDF.js**.
* Keep original files untouched.

---

# 14. Audit Log

Maintain an audit log for every action.

Example:

```text
2026-07-05 10:30 AM

Manager uploaded Dashboard.png

2026-07-05 10:35 AM

Manager generated OCR Report

2026-07-05 10:40 AM

Manager deleted Dashboard.png from UI

Backend File Status:

Available

Database Status:

Deleted

Physical File:

Still Exists
```

---

# Final Requirements

* Support all common image and document formats.
* Allow multiple file uploads in one project.
* Automatically create a backend folder using the project name.
* Save every uploaded file permanently in that project folder.
* Save OCR outputs, reports, and metadata inside the same project folder.
* **Deleting a file or project from the frontend must never physically delete the backend files.** Only update the database status (`isDeleted` or `ARCHIVED`).
* Design the solution using **Spring Boot + MySQL** with a scalable, secure, and production-ready architecture that follows enterprise best practices.
